# Canonical production environment reference.
# Copy to infra/.env, replace every CHANGE_ME value, and keep the file off git.
#
# Every assignment records its purpose, secret status, and rotation requirement.
# Values marked as secrets are blank (feature disabled) or unmistakable
# CHANGE_ME placeholders; none is a live-looking credential that should survive
# first boot.

# ── Compose-managed API/worker invariants ────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Documents the API/worker runtime mode; Compose pins it to production.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
NODE_ENV=production
# Purpose: Documents the internal API port coupled to the proxy and healthcheck.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
PORT=3000
# Purpose: Documents the shared durable export directory mounted in both processes.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_EXPORT_DIR=/var/lib/bettertrack/exports

# ── PostgreSQL and Redis ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Existing volumes: POSTGRES_PASSWORD is only consumed during first
# initialization; changing it and restarting cannot update the database role.
# Follow docs/ops.md "Database credential rotation" before changing either
# password value below.

# Purpose: Selects the PostgreSQL role created by the db container.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
POSTGRES_USER=bt
# Purpose: Authenticates the PostgreSQL role used by BetterTrack.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: use the staged existing-volume procedure in docs/ops.md.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_STRONG_PASSWORD
# Purpose: Selects the PostgreSQL database created by the db container.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
POSTGRES_DB=bettertrack
# Purpose: Connects the API and worker to PostgreSQL through the db service.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: update only after rotating the role, then recreate all database consumers.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://bt:CHANGE_ME_STRONG_PASSWORD@db:5432/bettertrack
# Purpose: Connects the API and worker to Redis through the redis service.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable for the credential-free stock Redis URL.
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

# ── Sessions and stored-record encryption ───────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Signs login-session cookies; comma-separated values support overlap.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: prepend a new 64-byte value, expire old sessions, then remove old values.
SESSION_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_64_RANDOM_HEX_BYTES
# Purpose: Identifies the active stored-record encryption key in ciphertext metadata.
# Secret: no. Rotation: change whenever BT_DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY changes.
BT_DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=initial-2026
# Purpose: Encrypts stored TOTP secrets and Discord webhook URLs.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: add the old key below, re-encrypt records, then retire it.
BT_DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_ME_64_RANDOM_HEX_BYTES
# Purpose: Supplies ordered id=key entries that decrypt records during key rotation.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: remove an old entry only after re-encryption reports no remaining use.
BT_DATA_ENCRYPTION_DECRYPT_KEYS=
# Purpose: Labels BetterTrack accounts inside authenticator applications.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable; changing it only changes newly issued labels.
TOTP_ISSUER=BetterTrack

# ── Deployment topology ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One scheme derives all public origins. In subdomains mode, terminate TLS in
# front of the proxy and point the apex plus api/web/admin/mobile DNS names at it.
# In ports mode, one host exposes the five BT_PORT_* values.

# Purpose: Chooses subdomains or ports topology.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_MODE=subdomains
# Purpose: Sets the base public domain or host used to derive every origin.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart the stack when changed.
BT_DOMAIN=track.example.at
# Purpose: Overrides the topology's derived TLS scheme; blank uses the mode default.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_TLS=
# Purpose: Sets the API subdomain label in subdomains mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart when changed.
BT_SUB_API=api
# Purpose: Sets the user-app subdomain label in subdomains mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart when changed.
BT_SUB_WEB=web
# Purpose: Sets the admin-app subdomain label in subdomains mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart when changed.
BT_SUB_ADMIN=admin
# Purpose: Sets the mobile-placeholder subdomain label in subdomains mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart when changed.
BT_SUB_MOBILE=mobile
# Purpose: Publishes the front proxy host port in subdomains mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_HTTP_PORT=80
# Purpose: Sets the API origin port in ports mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: restart the proxy and clients when changed.
BT_PORT_API=3000
# Purpose: Sets the user-app origin port in ports mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: restart the proxy when changed.
BT_PORT_WEB=8080
# Purpose: Sets the admin-app origin port in ports mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: restart the proxy when changed.
BT_PORT_ADMIN=8081
# Purpose: Sets the product-landing origin port in ports mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: restart the proxy when changed.
BT_PORT_PRODUCT=8082
# Purpose: Sets the mobile-placeholder origin port in ports mode.
# Secret: no. Rotation: restart the proxy when changed.
BT_PORT_MOBILE=8083
# Purpose: Overrides the derived API origin for split or legacy hosting.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update the proxy/TLS configuration and restart when changed.
BT_API_ORIGIN=
# Purpose: Overrides the derived user-app origin for split or legacy hosting.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update the proxy/TLS configuration and restart when changed.
BT_WEB_ORIGIN=
# Purpose: Overrides the derived admin-app origin for split hosting.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update the proxy/TLS configuration and restart when changed.
BT_ADMIN_ORIGIN=
# Purpose: Overrides the derived credential-free product-landing origin.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update the proxy/TLS configuration and restart when changed.
BT_PRODUCT_ORIGIN=
# Purpose: Overrides the derived credential-free mobile-placeholder origin.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update the proxy/TLS configuration and restart when changed.
BT_MOBILE_ORIGIN=

# ── Browser Google Drive client ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Bakes the public Drive appdata OAuth client id into the web image.
# Secret: no. Rotation: replace the client id and rebuild the web image when revoked.
VITE_GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Google sign-in and admin sessions ───────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Enables Google sign-in when paired with BT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET.
# Secret: no. Rotation: replace with the paired OAuth client when credentials rotate.
BT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Purpose: Authenticates BetterTrack's server-side Google sign-in exchange.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: rotate in Google, update here, and restart api and worker.
BT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Purpose: Sets the absolute admin-session lifetime in hours (allowed range 6-24).
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
ADMIN_SESSION_LIFETIME_HOURS=12

# ── Market data, intelligence, realtime, and request budgets ────────────────
# Purpose: Caps concurrent upstream market-provider calls per process.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
PROVIDER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# Purpose: Sets the minimum delay in milliseconds between provider call starts.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
PROVIDER_MIN_SPACING_MS=250
# Purpose: Enables the keyless Yahoo-to-Stooq market-data failover chain.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
MARKET_FAILOVER_ENABLED=false
# Purpose: Enables dividend, earnings, news, and split intelligence surfaces.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
MARKET_INTEL_ENABLED=true
# Purpose: Enables the Socket.IO realtime gateway; polling remains the fallback.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
REALTIME_ENABLED=true
# Purpose: Sets the short general-rate-limit burst window in seconds.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
RATE_LIMIT_BURST_WINDOW_SEC=10
# Purpose: Sets requests allowed inside the short burst window.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
RATE_LIMIT_BURST_LIMIT=60

# ── Email, Telegram/Discord, and push channels ───────────────────────────────
# Email stays disabled unless both SMTP_HOST and SMTP_FROM are set.

# Purpose: Selects the SMTP relay host.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
SMTP_HOST=
# Purpose: Selects the SMTP relay port (465 for implicit TLS).
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
SMTP_PORT=
# Purpose: Supplies the SMTP authentication username.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update with the relay account when credentials rotate.
SMTP_USER=
# Purpose: Supplies the SMTP authentication password or app password.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: rotate at the mail provider, update here, and restart.
SMTP_PASS=
# Purpose: Sets the sender address used for outbound BetterTrack email.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update with the mail identity when changed.
SMTP_FROM=
# Purpose: Authenticates the optional Telegram notification bot.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: revoke and replace through BotFather, then restart.
BT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Purpose: Globally enables the otherwise hidden Telegram and Discord channels.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_TELEGRAM_DISCORD_ENABLED=false
# Purpose: Points at a mounted FCM service-account JSON inside the containers.
# Secret: no. Rotation: rotate the referenced service-account key and replace the mounted file.
BT_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=
# Purpose: Publishes the browser-push VAPID public key.
# Secret: no. Rotation: replace together with the private key.
BT_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Purpose: Signs browser-push messages with the VAPID keypair.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: rotate as a pair; existing browser subscriptions may need renewal.
BT_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Purpose: Sets the browser-push contact URI; blank derives mailto:admin@BT_DOMAIN.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAPID_SUBJECT=

# ── Local AI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both Ollama values are optional; leaving either blank keeps AI surfaces hidden.

# Purpose: Sets the owner-LAN Ollama base URL used by the server.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable; update and restart when the endpoint moves.
BT_OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=
# Purpose: Selects the Ollama model used when no admin runtime override exists.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_OLLAMA_MODEL=
# Purpose: Caps each user's AI completions per UTC day by default.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_AI_DAILY_CAP=20

# ── MIRRORCHAIN and paranoid-vault limits ────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Caps active members in one MIRRORCHAIN group portfolio.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
MIRROR_MAX_MEMBERS=16
# Purpose: Caps one encrypted paranoid-vault envelope in bytes (default 16 MiB).
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAULT_MAX_BYTES=16777216
# Purpose: Caps retained encrypted vault versions.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAULT_HISTORY_MAX_VERSIONS=10
# Purpose: Caps encrypted vault-version age in days.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAULT_HISTORY_MAX_AGE_DAYS=30
# Purpose: Sets the paranoid-vault write-rate window in seconds.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAULT_RATE_WINDOW_SEC=60
# Purpose: Sets writes allowed per user inside the paranoid-vault rate window.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_VAULT_RATE_LIMIT=60

# ── Prometheus and Grafana ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The stack provisions both services. Host bindings default to loopback and are
# never routed through the public web proxy. See docs/monitoring.md for access options.

# Purpose: Enables the dedicated API and worker Prometheus listeners.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_METRICS_ENABLED=true
# Purpose: Binds metrics inside each container for Prometheus sidecar access.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable; keep 0.0.0.0 only inside the container network.
BT_METRICS_HOST=0.0.0.0
# Purpose: Sets the internal API and worker metrics-listener port.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_METRICS_PORT=9464
# Purpose: Binds Grafana and Prometheus host ports to loopback or a trusted LAN IP.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable; never use 0.0.0.0 on a public host.
BT_OBS_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Purpose: Publishes the Grafana host port on BT_OBS_BIND_HOST.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_GRAFANA_PORT=3001
# Purpose: Publishes the Prometheus host port on BT_OBS_BIND_HOST.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_PROMETHEUS_PORT=9090
# Purpose: Creates the local Grafana administrator username on first boot.
# Secret: no. Rotation: manage the account in Grafana after bootstrap.
BT_GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin
# Purpose: Creates and authenticates the local Grafana administrator.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: replace before first boot and rotate in Grafana if exposed.
BT_GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_BEFORE_FIRST_BOOT
# Purpose: Enables authenticated external Grafana access through the admin surface.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_OBS_EXTERNAL_ACCESS=false
# Purpose: Makes Grafana generate URLs below the admin-proxy subpath.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_GRAFANA_SERVE_FROM_SUB_PATH=false
# Purpose: Sets Grafana's externally visible root URL.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update with the public proxy URL when changed.
BT_GRAFANA_ROOT_URL=http://localhost:3000/
# Purpose: Allows Viewer access behind the already authenticated admin proxy.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_GRAFANA_ANON_ENABLED=false
# Purpose: Allows Grafana to render inside the admin Diagnostics iframe.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_GRAFANA_ALLOW_EMBEDDING=true
# Purpose: Advertises an optional auth-gated public Grafana origin to the admin UI.
# Secret: no. Rotation: update DNS/TLS and restart when changed.
BT_GRAFANA_PUBLIC_URL=
# Purpose: Sets the API's internal Grafana probe and proxy URL.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable unless the Compose service name changes.
BT_GRAFANA_INTERNAL_URL=http://grafana:3000
# Purpose: Sets the API's internal Prometheus probe URL.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable unless the Compose service name changes.
BT_PROMETHEUS_INTERNAL_URL=http://prometheus:9090

# ── Backups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Sets local pg_dump retention in the pgbackups volume, in days.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=14
# Purpose: Points at the host file containing the public age backup recipient.
# Secret: no. Rotation: replace after rotating the offline age identity.
BT_BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT_HOST_FILE=
# Purpose: Points at the host rclone.conf containing offsite OAuth credentials.
# Secret: no. Rotation: rotate credentials inside the referenced file and replace it.
BT_BACKUP_RCLONE_CONFIG_HOST_FILE=
# Purpose: Selects the rclone remote and path for encrypted offsite archives.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_BACKUP_RCLONE_REMOTE=
# Purpose: Sets encrypted offsite-backup retention in days.
# Secret: no. Rotation: not applicable.
BT_BACKUP_REMOTE_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# ── First admin (one-shot seed only) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Purpose: Selects the email address created by the first-admin seed.
# Secret: no. Rotation: manage the email in BetterTrack after bootstrap.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.at
# Purpose: Supplies the first-admin password to the one-shot seed.
# Secret: yes. Rotation: leave blank here; export a generated value only for seed.js.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
#
# Optional demo seed inputs are command-scoped rather than long-running service
# configuration. Keep them out of infra/.env and pass them only to the one-shot:
#   export BT_DEMO_PASSWORD="$(openssl rand -base64 24)"
#   docker compose run --rm -e BT_SEED_DEMO=true -e BT_DEMO_PASSWORD api \
#     node dist/scripts/seed.js
